/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 2:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain String Slicing, Negative Indexing, and Lexicographical String Comparison in Python with comprehensive code examples.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Slicing Mechanics & Substring Extraction:) Tj
T*
(   String slicing extracts a new substring using the slice syntax:) Tj
T*
(   s[start : stop : step]) Tj
T*
(   - start: Inclusive index \(defaults to 0 if step > 0, len\(s\) - 1 if step < 0\).) Tj
T*
(   - stop: Exclusive bound \(defaults to len\(s\) if step > 0, past origin if step < 0\).) Tj
T*
(   - step: Stride/increment \(positive = left-to-right, negative = right-to-left\).) Tj
T*
(   - Python automatically clamps slice indices within [0, len\(s\)] without throwing IndexError.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Negative Indexing Mechanics:) Tj
T*
(   Negative index -k refers to the element at physical index len\(s\) - k:) Tj
T*
(   - s[-1] is the last character.) Tj
T*
(   - s[-len\(s\)] is the first character.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Lexicographical Comparison:) Tj
T*
(   Python compares strings character-by-character from left to right using Unicode ordinals) Tj
T*
(   \(ord\(c\)\):) Tj
T*
(   - 'apple' < 'banana' \(since ord\('a'\)=97 < ord\('b'\)=98 -> True\).) Tj
T*
(   - 'Apple' < 'apple' \(since uppercase 'A'=65 < lowercase 'a'=97 -> True\).) Tj
T*
(   - 'app' < 'apple' \(shorter string is less than longer prefix extension\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Python Code Demonstration:) Tj
T*
(   def demonstrate_slicing_and_comparisons\(\):) Tj
T*
(   phrase = "ArtificialIntelligence") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   print\("--- Slicing Patterns ---"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Original: '{phrase}'"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"phrase[0:10]: '{phrase[0:10]}'"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"phrase[10:]: '{phrase[10:]}'"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"phrase[-12:]: '{phrase[-12:]}'"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"phrase[::2]: '{phrase[::2]}'"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"phrase[::-1]: '{phrase[::-1]}' \(Reversed\)"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   print\("\\n--- Lexicographical Comparisons ---"\)) Tj
T*
(   s1 = "Algorithm") Tj
T*
(   s2 = "algor") Tj
T*
ET

endstream
