(>> Solution to Question 4:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Python Lists: Dynamic Array Architecture, Memory Allocation, Mutability, and In-Place Mutation versus Rebinding.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. CPython List Architecture \(Dynamic Array of Pointers\):) Tj
T*
(   In CPython, a list is NOT a linked list! It is implemented as a PyListObject containing:) Tj
T*
(   1. ob_size: Number of elements currently in the list \(len\(L\)\).) Tj
T*
(   2. allocated: Total capacity of the internal contiguous C pointer array \(ob_item\).) Tj
T*
(   3. ob_item: Pointer to an array of pointers \(PyObject**\) referencing items on the heap.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Overallocation & Amortized O\(1\) Growth:) Tj
T*
(   When append\(\) exceeds allocated capacity, CPython reallocates the array with an overallocation) Tj
T*
(   growth factor:) Tj
T*
(   allocated = \(size + \(size >> 3\) + \(size < 9 ? 3 : 6\)\)) Tj
T*
(   This geometric expansion guarantees that appending N elements takes O\(N\) total time, achieving) Tj
T*
(   Amortized O\(1\) per append!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. In-Place Mutation vs Variable Rebinding:) Tj
T*
(   - In-Place Mutation: Operations like L.append\(x\), L.extend\(items\), L[i] = v, and L.sort\(\)) Tj
T*
(   modify the existing heap object directly without changing id\(L\).) Tj
T*
(   - Rebinding: Operations like L = L + [x] allocate a brand new list and rebind variable L to the) Tj
T*
(   new object's memory address.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Python Code Demonstration:) Tj
T*
(   import sys) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def trace_list_growth\(\):) Tj
T*
(   """Observe CPython dynamic overallocation in action.""") Tj
T*
(   nums = []) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"{'Length':<10}{'Capacity \(Bytes\)':<18}{'Growth Event':<20}"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\("-" * 48\)) Tj
T*
(   prev_size = sys.getsizeof\(nums\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   for i in range\(25\):) Tj
T*
(   nums.append\(i\)) Tj
T*
(   current_size = sys.getsizeof\(nums\)) Tj
T*
(   if current_size != prev_size or i == 0:) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"{len\(nums\):<10}{current_size:<18}{'Reallocation!':<20}"\)) Tj
T*
(   prev_size = current_size) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   trace_list_growth\(\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Demonstrating Mutation vs Rebinding) Tj
T*
(   lst1 = [10, 20]) Tj
T*
(   orig_id = id\(lst1\)) Tj
T*
(   lst1.append\(30\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"\\nIn-Place Append -> ID Unchanged: {id\(lst1\) == orig_id}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   lst1 = lst1 + [40] # Rebinding) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
endobj
