12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain List Comprehensions in Python. Contrast list comprehensions with map\(\), filter\(\), and explicit for loops in readability, bytecode, and performance.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Theoretical Basis of List Comprehensions:) Tj
T*
(   Codified in PEP 202, list comprehensions provide a concise, declarative mathematical) Tj
T*
(   set-builder syntax for constructing lists:) Tj
T*
(   Syntax: [expression for item in iterable if condition]) Tj
T*
(   Comprehensions combine mapping \(expression\) and filtering \(if condition\) into a unified) Tj
T*
(   construct.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Performance and Bytecode Superiority:) Tj
T*
(   - Explicit for-loop: Repeatedly calls the list.append attribute lookup in Python bytecode on) Tj
T*
(   every iteration, incurring dictionary lookup overhead.) Tj
T*
(   - List Comprehension: Compiles into specialized C-level bytecode \(LIST_APPEND opcode\) that) Tj
T*
(   directly appends to the internal C array without Python attribute lookup overhead.) Tj
T*
(   - map\(\) / filter\(\): Return lazy iterators; converting them via list\(map\(...\)\) requires function) Tj
T*
(   call overhead for every element unless using C built-ins.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Python Code Demonstration:) Tj
T*
(   import dis) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # 1. Comparative Implementations) Tj
T*
(   dataset = range\(1, 11\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Method A: Traditional Loop) Tj
T*
(   loop_res = []) Tj
T*
(   for x in dataset:) Tj
T*
(   if x % 2 == 0:) Tj
T*
(   loop_res.append\(x ** 2\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Method B: List Comprehension) Tj
T*
(   comp_res = [x ** 2 for x in dataset if x % 2 == 0]) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Method C: map and filter) Tj
T*
(   mf_res = list\(map\(lambda x: x ** 2, filter\(lambda x: x % 2 == 0, dataset\)\)\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Comprehension Result: {comp_res} \(Matches Loop: {comp_res == loop_res == mf_res}\)"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # 2. Nested List Comprehension \(Matrix Flattening\)) Tj
T*
(   matrix = [[1, 2, 3], [4, 5, 6], [7, 8, 9]]) Tj
T*
(   flattened = [val for row in matrix for val in row]) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Flattened Matrix: {flattened}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # 3. Conditional Value Mapping \(if-else inside expression\)) Tj
T*
(   parity = ["Even" if x % 2 == 0 else "Odd" for x in range\(5\)]) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Parity Classification: {parity}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Complexity Analysis:) Tj
T*
ET

