12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Parameter Passing in Python: 'Pass-by-Object-Reference' \(Call-by-Sharing\). Demonstrate how mutating mutable parameters affects caller state.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Theoretical Paradigm: Pass-by-Object-Reference:) Tj
T*
(   Python does NOT use traditional 'pass-by-value' \(copying data\) or 'pass-by-reference' \(alias to) Tj
T*
(   variable\).) Tj
T*
(   Instead, Python strictly adheres to Pass-by-Object-Reference \(Call-by-Sharing\):) Tj
T*
(   - Every argument passed into a function is an object reference \(pointer\).) Tj
T*
(   - The parameter inside the function receives a copy of the pointer pointing to the exact same) Tj
T*
(   heap object.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Behavioral Consequences:) Tj
T*
(   - If the argument is an Immutable Object \(int, str, tuple\): The function cannot modify the) Tj
T*
(   caller's object. Any modification rebinds the local parameter to a new object, leaving the) Tj
T*
(   caller unaffected.) Tj
T*
(   - If the argument is a Mutable Object \(list, dict, set\): In-place mutations \(e.g.,) Tj
T*
(   param.append\(\), param[k]=v\) directly alter the underlying heap object, mutating the caller's) Tj
T*
(   state!) Tj
T*
(   - Rebinding a Mutable Parameter \(param = [1, 2, 3]\): Redirects the local pointer to a new heap) Tj
T*
(   object, severing the connection to caller's object.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Python Code Demonstration:) Tj
T*
(   def mutate_vs_rebind\(shared_list: list, local_rebind: list\):) Tj
T*
(   # In-place mutation affects caller!) Tj
T*
(   shared_list.append\("MUTATED_IN_PLACE"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Rebinding affects only local parameter!) Tj
T*
(   local_rebind = ["NEW_OBJECT"]) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Inside Function: local_rebind = {local_rebind}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   orig_list1 = [1, 2]) Tj
T*
(   orig_list2 = ['A', 'B']) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Before Function Call: list1 = {orig_list1}, list2 = {orig_list2}"\)) Tj
T*
(   mutate_vs_rebind\(orig_list1, orig_list2\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"After Function Call: list1 = {orig_list1} \(Mutated!\)"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"After Function Call: list2 = {orig_list2} \(Unaffected by rebinding!\)"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Memory Model Trace:) Tj
T*
(   - Function Entry: shared_list and orig_list1 both hold pointer 0x7fa0.) Tj
T*
(   shared_list.append modifies heap at 0x7fa0. Caller sees change.) Tj
T*
(   - local_rebind initially holds pointer 0x81b0.) Tj
T*
(   local_rebind = ['NEW_OBJECT'] allocates 0x95c0 and points local_rebind to 0x95c0.) Tj
T*
(   orig_list2 remains pointing to 0x81b0.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   5. Complexity Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   - Parameter Passing Overhead: O\(1\) pointer copy.) Tj
T*
(   - Space Complexity: O\(1\) frame reference.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

endstream
