12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Tuples in Python: Immutability, Creation, Single-Element Gotcha, Tuple Packing, Unpacking, and Functions Returning Multiple Values.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Tuple Architecture & Immutability:) Tj
T*
(   A tuple \(tuple\) is an immutable ordered sequence of object references.) Tj
T*
(   Key Characteristics:) Tj
T*
(   - Defined with parentheses \(\) or comma-separated values.) Tj
T*
(   - Memory Efficient: Tuples require less memory overhead than lists because their size is fixed) Tj
T*
(   at instantiation. CPython pre-allocates small tuple caches.) Tj
T*
(   - Hashable: If all constituent elements of a tuple are immutable, the tuple itself is hashable) Tj
T*
(   and can serve as a dictionary key or set element.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. The Single-Element Tuple Gotcha:) Tj
T*
(   Writing t = \(5\) evaluates to the integer 5 because parentheses are parsed as mathematical) Tj
T*
(   grouping operators.) Tj
T*
(   To define a single-element tuple, a trailing comma is syntactically mandatory:) Tj
T*
(   t = \(5,\) or t = 5,) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Tuple Packing, Sequence Unpacking, and Return Values:) Tj
T*
(   - Packing: x = 10, 20, 30 packs integers into tuple \(10, 20, 30\).) Tj
T*
(   - Unpacking: a, b, c = x unpacks elements into separate variables.) Tj
T*
(   - Extended Unpacking \(PEP 3132\): first, *middle, last = sequence.) Tj
T*
(   - Multiple Return Values: A function returning return x, y, z is actually returning a single) Tj
T*
(   packed tuple \(x, y, z\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Python Code Demonstration:) Tj
T*
(   # 1. Single element tuple verification) Tj
T*
(   not_a_tuple = \(42\)) Tj
T*
(   valid_tuple = \(42,\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"type\(\(42\)\): {type\(not_a_tuple\).__name__} | type\(\(42,\)\): {type\(valid_tuple\).__name__}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # 2. Returning multiple values from function) Tj
T*
(   def compute_statistics\(numbers: list\):) Tj
T*
(   min_val = min\(numbers\)) Tj
T*
(   max_val = max\(numbers\)) Tj
T*
(   mean_val = sum\(numbers\) / len\(numbers\)) Tj
T*
(   return min_val, max_val, mean_val # Returns a packed 3-tuple) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   stats = compute_statistics\([10, 25, 4, 88, 32]\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Stats Tuple: {stats} | Type: {type\(stats\).__name__}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Unpacking stats) Tj
T*
(   low, high, avg = stats) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Unpacked: Min={low}, Max={high}, Mean={avg:.2f}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # 3. Extended Unpacking) Tj
T*
(   head, *tail = [100, 200, 300, 400]) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Head: {head} | Tail: {tail}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   5. Complexity Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   - Unpacking Time Complexity: O\(K\) where K is number of unpacked elements.) Tj
T*
(   - Space Complexity: O\(1\) register assignments.) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
