(>> Solution to Question 9:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Python Dictionaries: Hash Table Architecture, Key Hashability, Collision Resolution, and Compact Dict Memory Layout.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Hash Table Architecture of Python Dictionaries:) Tj
T*
(   A dictionary \(dict\) is an associative array mapping unique keys to arbitrary values.) Tj
T*
(   Key Architecture:) Tj
T*
(   - Hash Function: When a key k is accessed, Python calls hash\(k\) to generate an integer hash) Tj
T*
(   code.) Tj
T*
(   - Bucket Indexing: The hash code is masked with the table size to determine the starting bucket) Tj
T*
(   index: idx = hash\(k\) & \(size - 1\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Key Hashability Requirements:) Tj
T*
(   A key must be Hashable:) Tj
T*
(   1. Must implement __hash__\(\) returning an invariant integer across its lifespan.) Tj
T*
(   2. Must implement __eq__\(\) to compare equality.) Tj
T*
(   3. If two objects are equal \(a == b\), their hash codes MUST be identical \(hash\(a\) == hash\(b\)\).) Tj
T*
(   Mutable types \(list, dict, set\) are unhashable because in-place mutation would change their) Tj
T*
(   hash, corrupting the hash table.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Collision Resolution via Open Addressing:) Tj
T*
(   When two keys hash to the same bucket, CPython uses Open Addressing with pseudo-random) Tj
T*
(   perturbation probing:) Tj
T*
(   idx = \(5 * idx + 1 + perturb\) & \(size - 1\)) Tj
T*
(   This probe sequence visits all table entries while avoiding primary clustering.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Python 3.6+ Compact Dict Design:) Tj
T*
(   Traditional hash tables stored sparse arrays containing [hash, key, value] tuples, wasting 60%) Tj
T*
(   of memory on empty slots.) Tj
T*
(   Modern CPython separates the table into:) Tj
T*
(   1. Dense 'entries' array: Stores [hash, key, value] contiguously in insertion order.) Tj
T*
(   2. Sparse 'indices' array: Stores tiny integers \(int8/int16\) indexing into the dense entries) Tj
T*
(   array.) Tj
T*
(   This achieves 25% memory reduction and guarantees Insertion-Order Preservation!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   5. Python Code Demonstration:) Tj
T*
(   # Verification of hashability and dictionary operations) Tj
T*
(   class Coordinate:) Tj
T*
(   def __init__\(self, x, y\):) Tj
T*
(   self.x = x) Tj
T*
(   self.y = y) Tj
T*
(   def __hash__\(self\):) Tj
T*
(   return hash\(\(self.x, self.y\)\)) Tj
T*
(   def __eq__\(self, other\):) Tj
T*
(   return isinstance\(other, Coordinate\) and \(self.x, self.y\) == \(other.x, other.y\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   c1 = Coordinate\(10, 20\)) Tj
T*
(   c2 = Coordinate\(10, 20\)) Tj
T*
(   geo_cache = {c1: "Sensor_Node_Alpha"}) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   print\(f"c1 == c2: {c1 == c2} | hash\(c1\) == hash\(c2\): {hash\(c1\) == hash\(c2\)}"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Lookup via c2: {geo_cache[c2]} \(Hash table hit!\)"\)) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
