BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Sparse Matrices. Compare traditional 2D nested list representation with Dictionary of Keys \(DOK\) in memory footprint and retrieval efficiency.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Theoretical Principles of Sparse Matrices:) Tj
T*
(   A sparse matrix is a matrix in which the overwhelming majority of elements are zero.) Tj
T*
(   In scientific computing, graph adjacency matrices, and machine learning recommendation engines,) Tj
T*
(   matrices often exceed 1,000,000 x 1,000,000 in dimensions, with < 0.01% non-zero entries.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Traditional 2D Nested List vs Dictionary of Keys \(DOK\):) Tj
T*
(   - Traditional 2D List \(Dense\): Allocates memory for every single cell \(including all zeros\). An) Tj
T*
(   N x N matrix requires O\(N^2\) memory. For N = 100,000, storing 10 billion elements causes) Tj
T*
(   Out-Of-Memory \(OOM\) crashes.) Tj
T*
(   - Dictionary of Keys \(DOK\): Stores ONLY the non-zero elements, mapping coordinate tuples \(row,) Tj
T*
(   col\) to values: {\(r, c\): value}.) Tj
T*
(   Memory complexity drops to O\(K\) where K is the number of non-zero entries \(K << N^2\).) Tj
T*
(   Missing keys implicitly represent 0.0, retrieved in O\(1\) time via dok.get\(\(r, c\), 0.0\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Python Implementation:) Tj
T*
(   class SparseMatrixDOK:) Tj
T*
(   def __init__\(self, num_rows: int, num_cols: int\):) Tj
T*
(   self.rows = num_rows) Tj
T*
(   self.cols = num_cols) Tj
T*
(   self._data = {} # Dictionary of Keys) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def set\(self, r: int, c: int, value: float\):) Tj
T*
(   if not \(0 <= r < self.rows and 0 <= c < self.cols\):) Tj
T*
(   raise IndexError\("Matrix coordinate out of bounds."\)) Tj
T*
(   if value != 0:) Tj
T*
(   self._data[\(r, c\)] = value) Tj
T*
(   elif \(r, c\) in self._data:) Tj
T*
(   del self._data[\(r, c\)] # Remove zero entries to conserve memory) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def get\(self, r: int, c: int\) -> float:) Tj
T*
(   return self._data.get\(\(r, c\), 0.0\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def non_zero_count\(self\) -> int:) Tj
T*
(   return len\(self._data\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Demonstration with large virtual matrix \(10,000 x 10,000\)) Tj
T*
(   sparse_mat = SparseMatrixDOK\(10_000, 10_000\)) Tj
T*
(   sparse_mat.set\(42, 108, 3.14159\)) Tj
T*
(   sparse_mat.set\(999, 5000, 42.0\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Virtual Matrix Dimensions: {sparse_mat.rows} x {sparse_mat.cols} \(100 Million Cells!\)"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Actually Stored Non-Zero Entries: {sparse_mat.non_zero_count\(\)} entries"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Element at \(42, 108\): {sparse_mat.get\(42, 108\)}"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Element at \(0, 0\) [Zero]: {sparse_mat.get\(0, 0\)}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Complexity Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   - Dense List Space: O\(R * C\).) Tj
T*
(   - Sparse DOK Space: O\(K\) where K is non-zero elements.) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
