/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Aliasing, Shallow Copy, and Deep Copy in Python. Analyze the copy module \(copy\(\) vs deepcopy\(\)\) with memory address diagrams and nested mutation traces.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Object References and Aliasing:) Tj
T*
(   In Python, assigning b = a does NOT copy the object; it merely creates an Alias - a second) Tj
T*
(   variable pointing to the exact same heap memory address \(id\(b\) == id\(a\)\).) Tj
T*
(   Mutating b modifies a simultaneously.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Shallow Copy vs Deep Copy:) Tj
T*
(   - Shallow Copy \(copy.copy\(x\), list.copy\(\), or x[:]\): Creates a new outer container object, but) Tj
T*
(   populates it with references to the exact same nested child objects.) Tj
T*
(   Modifying a primitive element in the outer container does not affect the original, but mutating) Tj
T*
(   a nested child object DOES affect the original!) Tj
T*
(   - Deep Copy \(copy.deepcopy\(x\)\): Recursively creates a new outer container AND recursively) Tj
T*
(   clones all nested objects, lists, and dictionaries. The clone is 100% physically decoupled from) Tj
T*
(   the original.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Python Code Demonstration:) Tj
T*
(   import copy) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Original nested list) Tj
T*
(   original = [[1, 2], [3, 4]]) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # 1. Aliasing) Tj
T*
(   alias = original) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # 2. Shallow Copy) Tj
T*
(   shallow = copy.copy\(original\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # 3. Deep Copy) Tj
T*
(   deep = copy.deepcopy\(original\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Perform mutations) Tj
T*
(   original.append\([5, 6]\) # Mutates top-level list) Tj
T*
(   original[0][0] = 999 # Mutates nested child list) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   print\("--- State After Mutations ---"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Original: {original} \(id: {id\(original\)}\)"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Alias: {alias} \(Tracks ALL changes; id: {id\(alias\)}\)"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Shallow: {shallow} \(Outer unaffected, but nested [0][0] was mutated!\)"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Deep: {deep} \(Completely isolated; zero mutations!\)"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Memory Model Diagram:) Tj
T*
(   Original -> Heap 0x1000 [ ptr -> 0x2000 [1, 2], ptr -> 0x3000 [3, 4] ]) Tj
T*
(   Shallow -> Heap 0x4000 [ ptr -> 0x2000 [1, 2], ptr -> 0x3000 [3, 4] ] \(Shared children!\)) Tj
T*
(   Deep -> Heap 0x5000 [ ptr -> 0x6000 [1, 2], ptr -> 0x7000 [3, 4] ] \(Cloned children!\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   5. Complexity Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   - Shallow Copy Time: O\(N\) outer elements copy.) Tj
T*
(   - Deep Copy Time: O\(Total Nodes\) recursive graph traversal with memoization table.) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
endobj
