(   [Problem Statement]: Design an Anagram Grouping program in Python using dictionaries, sorted string keys, or character frequency tuples.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Problem Context:) Tj
T*
(   Given an array of strings, group all anagrams together into sublists.) Tj
T*
(   Two strings are anagrams if they contain the identical multiset of characters with identical) Tj
T*
(   frequencies \(e.g., 'eat', 'tea', 'ate'\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Algorithmic Approaches:) Tj
T*
(   - Approach 1 \(Sorted Key\): Sort each word alphabetically \(sorted\('tea'\) -> 'aet'\). Use the) Tj
T*
(   sorted string as dictionary key: anagram_map['aet'].append\(word\).) Tj
T*
(   Time Complexity: O\(N * K log K\) where N is word count and K is max word length.) Tj
T*
(   - Approach 2 \(Character Frequency Tuple Key\): Count character frequencies \(size 26 tuple\) as) Tj
T*
(   dictionary key.) Tj
T*
(   Time Complexity: O\(N * K\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Python Implementation:) Tj
T*
(   from collections import defaultdict) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def group_anagrams_sorted_key\(words: list\) -> list:) Tj
T*
(   groups = defaultdict\(list\)) Tj
T*
(   for word in words:) Tj
T*
(   # Canonical signature key) Tj
T*
(   sorted_sig = "".join\(sorted\(word\)\)) Tj
T*
(   groups[sorted_sig].append\(word\)) Tj
T*
(   return list\(groups.values\(\)\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Verification) Tj
T*
(   word_list = ["eat", "tea", "tan", "ate", "nat", "bat", "listen", "silent"]) Tj
T*
(   grouped = group_anagrams_sorted_key\(word_list\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   print\("Original Words:", word_list\)) Tj
T*
(   print\("Grouped Anagrams:"\)) Tj
T*
(   for group in grouped:) Tj
T*
(   print\(" ", group\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Complexity Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   - Time Complexity: O\(N * K log K\) where K is string length.) Tj
T*
(   - Space Complexity: O\(N * K\) memory for grouping dictionary.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
