(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the collections.defaultdict type. Contrast standard dict.setdefault\(\) with defaultdict and demonstrate grouping applications.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Motivation for defaultdict:) Tj
T*
(   When building grouping dictionaries \(e.g., mapping category -> list of items\), standard) Tj
T*
(   dictionaries raise a KeyError if a key has not yet been initialized.) Tj
T*
(   Developers must write defensive code:) Tj
T*
(   if key not in d: d[key] = []) Tj
T*
(   d[key].append\(item\)) Tj
T*
(   or use d.setdefault\(key, []\).append\(item\), which constructs an empty list on every call) Tj
T*
(   regardless of necessity.) Tj
T*
(   collections.defaultdict\(default_factory\) automatically calls the default_factory callable) Tj
T*
(   \(e.g., list, int, set\) to instantiate and store a default value on the very first access of any) Tj
T*
(   missing key!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Python Code Demonstration:) Tj
T*
(   from collections import defaultdict) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # 1. Grouping Employees by Department) Tj
T*
