(   [Problem Statement]: Implement a String Permutation and Combination generator in Python without external libraries using recursive backtracking and list swapping.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Theoretical Formulation of Permutations:) Tj
T*
(   Given a string of unique characters \(e.g., 'ABC'\), generate all N! permutations:) Tj
T*
(   Permutations are formed by fixing each character at index 0 and recursively generating) Tj
T*
(   permutations of the remaining N - 1 characters.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Python Implementation:) Tj
T*
(   def generate_permutations\(chars: list, index=0, results=None\):) Tj
T*
(   if results is None:) Tj
T*
(   results = []) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   if index == len\(chars\):) Tj
T*
(   results.append\("".join\(chars\)\)) Tj
T*
(   return results) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   for i in range\(index, len\(chars\)\):) Tj
T*
(   # Swap characters to fix char at current index) Tj
T*
(   chars[index], chars[i] = chars[i], chars[index]) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Recursive call for remaining characters) Tj
T*
(   generate_permutations\(chars, index + 1, results\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

endstream
