(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the collections.ChainMap class in Python. How does it search across multiple chained dictionaries and how do updates behave?) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Architecture of ChainMap:) Tj
T*
(   Introduced in Python 3.3, collections.ChainMap groups multiple dictionaries or mappings) Tj
T*
(   together to create a single, updateable view.) Tj
T*
(   Instead of copying and merging multiple dictionaries into a new dict \(d1 | d2\), ChainMap stores) Tj
T*
(   references to the original mappings in an internal list \(self.maps\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Lookup and Write Semantics:) Tj
T*
(   - Read Lookups: Searches dictionaries sequentially in order \(maps[0], maps[1], maps[2]...\).) Tj
T*
(   Returns the first match found.) Tj
T*
(   - Mutations \(Insert, Update, Delete\): All write operations affect ONLY the first mapping in the) Tj
T*
(   chain \(maps[0]\)!) Tj
T*
(   Ideal for managing hierarchical configuration scopes: CLI args -> Environment variables ->) Tj
T*
(   Configuration file -> Hardcoded defaults.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Python Code Demonstration:) Tj
T*
(   from collections import ChainMap) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Configuration scopes) Tj
T*
(   hardcoded_defaults = {"theme": "light", "port": 8080, "debug": False}) Tj
T*
(   config_file = {"theme": "dark", "port": 9000}) Tj
T*
(   cli_overrides = {"debug": True}) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Chain the mappings) Tj
T*
(   app_config = ChainMap\(cli_overrides, config_file, hardcoded_defaults\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   print\("Layered Configuration Lookup:"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f" debug: {app_config['debug']} \(Overridden by CLI\)"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f" port: {app_config['port']} \(Overridden by Config File\)"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f" theme: {app_config['theme']} \(Overridden by Config File\)"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Mutating ChainMap) Tj
T*
(   app_config['new_setting'] = 'active') Tj
T*
(   print\(f"\\nAfter Adding 'new_setting':"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f" cli_overrides \(maps[0]\): {cli_overrides} \(Modified directly!\)"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f" config_file \(maps[1]\): {config_file} \(Completely untouched!\)"\)) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
endobj
