(>> Solution to Question 28:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Implement an In-Memory Inverted Index for a Document Search Engine using Python dictionaries and sets.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Problem Context:) Tj
T*
(   An inverted index is the fundamental data structure used by search engines \(e.g.,) Tj
T*
(   Elasticsearch, Google\).) Tj
T*
(   It maps words \(terms\) to the set of document IDs in which they appear, enabling sub-millisecond) Tj
T*
(   multi-word boolean searches \(AND, OR\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Python Implementation:) Tj
T*
(   import string) Tj
T*
(   from collections import defaultdict) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   class InvertedIndexEngine:) Tj
T*
(   def __init__\(self\):) Tj
T*
(   self.index = defaultdict\(set\)) Tj
T*
(   self.documents = {}) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def add_document\(self, doc_id: int, content: str\):) Tj
T*
(   self.documents[doc_id] = content) Tj
T*
(   # Clean and tokenize) Tj
T*
(   words = content.lower\(\).translate\(str.maketrans\('', '', string.punctuation\)\).split\(\)) Tj
T*
(   for w in set\(words\):) Tj
T*
(   self.index[w].add\(doc_id\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def search_and\(self, *query_terms\) -> list:) Tj
T*
(   """Find documents containing ALL query terms \(Intersection\).""") Tj
T*
(   if not query_terms:) Tj
T*
(   return []) Tj
T*
(   term_sets = [self.index.get\(t.lower\(\), set\(\)\) for t in query_terms]) Tj
T*
(   # Intersect all sets) Tj
T*
(   matching_doc_ids = set.intersection\(*term_sets\) if term_sets else set\(\)) Tj
T*
(   return [\(doc_id, self.documents[doc_id]\) for doc_id in matching_doc_ids]) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Verification) Tj
T*
(   engine = InvertedIndexEngine\(\)) Tj
T*
(   engine.add_document\(1, "Python is a high-level programming language."\)) Tj
T*
(   engine.add_document\(2, "Data structures and algorithms in Python."\)) Tj
T*
(   engine.add_document\(3, "Machine learning algorithms with neural networks."\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   results = engine.search_and\("algorithms", "python"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\("Search Query: ['algorithms' AND 'python'] -> Matches:"\)) Tj
T*
(   for doc_id, text in results:) Tj
T*
(   print\(f" Doc #{doc_id}: '{text}'"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Complexity Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   - Ingestion Time: O\(D * W\) where D is documents and W is words.) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
endobj
